# nr-office-ooxml-sheet-xml: integration fragment

Four modules of the existing crate mixdog-ooxml (native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml): sheet_styles (portable-sheet-styles.mjs),
sheet_xml (portable-sheet-xml.mjs), xlsx_cell_values (portable-xlsx-cell-values.mjs) and sheet_parts (portable-sheet-parts.mjs).
No protocol method, service or SERVICE_PENDING name belongs to it. No new Cargo dependency edge (the modules use mixdog-js,
mixdog-office-base and serde_json, which the crate already lists; the twin test uses mixdog-fsio, tempfile and
mixdog-office-base/test-support, also already listed). Not compiled (no cargo in this wave); the crate is already a workspace
member, so only the module lines below are needed.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml/src/lib.rs

lib.rs belongs to nr-office-ooxml-package, so it is not edited here. In the module list add, keeping the list alphabetical:

    pub mod sheet_parts;
    pub mod sheet_styles;
    pub mod sheet_xml;

(after `pub mod relations;`) and

    pub mod xlsx_cell_values;

(after `pub mod xml;`, before `pub mod zipio;`). In the crate doc, after the list that ends "... the placeholder scan
([`placeholder_scan`]) and the document fingerprint ([`fingerprint`])." add: "Worksheets: styles.xml ([`sheet_styles`]),
sheet and workbook XML ([`sheet_xml`]), what a cell shows ([`xlsx_cell_values`]) and the parts a sheet owns ([`sheet_parts`])."

## native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json

In the "sets" list, in sorted position by set name: immediately before the entry whose "set" is "office-stats" (after
"office-measure" and after any office-p... / office-q... set the wave adds), add:

    {
      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-sheet-xml.mjs --tree <tree>",
      "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-sheet-xml/MANIFEST.json",
      "manifestSha256": "68ff5bbd59ac3aae292ad188c929bfdd249bfc6a9685fca8c2f7b6d4b8ff629f",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-sheet-xml.mjs",
      "set": "office-sheet-xml",
      "totalBytes": 518767
    }

(The manifest hash is of native/core/fixtures/office-sheet-xml/MANIFEST.json as committed; recompute it with sha256 if the set is
recorded again.)

## Test run

    cargo test -p mixdog-ooxml --test twin_sheet_xml
    cargo test -p mixdog-ooxml --lib sheet_

The crate-local tests are in the four modules (cfg(test) mod tests): colours and style de-duplication, borders, indents, number
formats, section order, merged cells, row and column shifts, scale rules, views, areas, column widths, defined names, date text,
the protection hash, drawings and notes (including the portable-dollar-text cases for package parts and notes).
